          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em codiscrete groupoid
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are the elements of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            and which has a
            %em
              unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            for every ordered pair of objects.
          %p
            This is also called the
            %strong pair groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and sometimes also the
            %strong chaotic groupoid
            (this is explained
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Adjointness"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %strong indiscrete groupoid
            %strong coarse groupoid
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brandt+groupoid"} Brandt groupoid
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #CodiscreteGroupoid.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (codiscrete groupoid)
              %br/
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Set
              %strong codiscrete groupoid
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Codisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 1
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Codisc(X)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    X \times X
                    \\underoverset
                    {pr_2}
                    {pr_1}
                    {\rightrightarrows}
                    X
            %p whose object of objects is
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Obj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(X) = X
                ,
            %p
              whose objects of morphisms is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with itself
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(X) = X \times X
                ,
            %p
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
              morphism are the two canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projections"} projections
              out of the product, and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              operation is the unique one compatible with this:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi pr
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \times X \times X
                    \\xrightarrow{\; (pr_1, pr_3) \; }
                    X \times X
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CodiscreteGroupoid"}
              manifestly makes sense in the generality of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoids"} internal groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to any category with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              (in fact only
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
              are involved in the definition of codiscrete groupoids).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every codiscrete groupoid on an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
                is
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+space"} contractible
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+groupoid"} terminal groupoid
                (the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+algebra"} category algebra
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Codisc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Codisc(X)
                is the algebra of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\times n
                matrices. The contractibility of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Codisc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Codisc(X)
                is reflected in the fact that this algebra is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalent
                to the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              %p
                This maybe serves to illustrate: even though codiscrete groupoids are pretty trivial, they are not too trivial to be entirely without interest. Often it is useful to have big puffed-up versions of the point available (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
                of a codiscrete groupoid is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+graph"} complete graph
                (in that there is one
                %em and only one
                edge between any ordered pair of vertices).
          %h3#Adjointness Adjointness
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            is related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          %svg{:height => "51.584", :viewbox => "0 0 192.273 51.584", :width => "192.273", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
